  - question: "Do Appwrite's TanStack Start edge rules count toward my Firewall rule limit?"
    answer: "No. The two rules are built into Appwrite Cloud's edge and apply to every site automatically. They do not appear in your rules list and do not count toward your plan's [rule limit](/docs/products/firewall/rules#plan-limits)."
  - question: "Why does my TanStack Start site return 403 on a /_serverFn/ request?"
    answer: "Check the `X-Appwrite-WAF-Rule` response header. If it reads `internal-tanstack-start-server-fn-xss-header` or `internal-tanstack-start-server-fn-xss-navigation`, Appwrite's edge rule denied the request because it had no `x-tsr-serverFn: true` header or looked like a page load. The usual cause is an HTML form that posts straight to a server-function URL without JavaScript."
  - question: "Does self-hosted Appwrite include the TanStack Start edge rules?"
    answer: "No. The rules run on Appwrite Cloud's edge. On a self-hosted instance, upgrading TanStack Start is the fix. You can also add the same header and navigation checks to the reverse proxy in front of your sites."
